feat(flow-writer): implement local next-word suggestion strip

Replace the sample plugin with Flow Writer, a local writing assistant
backed by a llama.cpp server (raw /completion, base model, no template).

- src/llama.ts: /completion client + pure helpers; top-token probe
  (n_predict:1, n_probs) and greedy continuation used to complete token
  fragments into whole words and to deepen candidates. Tolerates old and
  new llama-server response shapes. window.fetch for AbortSignal support.
- src/controller.ts: SuggestionController — single live session with
  id-guarded staleness checks, AbortController per beat, LRU prompt
  cache (preserves deepened state), idle deepening one word per tick,
  stops at max depth / sentence end / dry model. DOM-free, fully tested.
- src/strip.ts: quiet fixed-position overlay strip below the cursor
  line; updates candidate text nodes in place, never reflows the doc.
- src/main.ts: CM6 update listener detects typed trigger chars, clears
  on any other edit/cursor move/blur; Alt+1..0 and click pick; pick
  inserts word + trailing space and naturally re-triggers; Escape
  dismisses. Only the focused editor owns a strip.
- src/settings.ts: endpoint, trigger chars, idle interval, max depth,
  candidate count.
- tests/: 20 vitest cases covering parsing, word completion, one-beat
  lifetime, abort safety, deepening, cache LRU, unreachable server.
- chore: manifest/package renamed to flow-writer, vitest added,
  CLAUDE.md with hard rules and key design decisions.

Note: origin still points at obsidianmd/obsidian-sample-plugin; push
skipped until a proper remote exists.
